      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n1. Many unused imports cluttering the file\n2. Cryptic variable name `b`\n3. The expected value `2 + 3 * 256 + 4 * 256 * 256` is opaque — it's the manual little-endian assembly of bytes at offsets 1–3\n\nI'll write an improved version with cleaner imports, descriptive naming, and a named constant that explains the expected value.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports, renames the cryptic `b` variable to `inputBytes`, extracts the expected value into a named `expectedValue` constant, and adds a brief comment explaining how the little-endian bytes map to the numeric result — all without changing the method calls or expected outcomes."
